<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="h-full">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Sourcebox" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">

    <%# Required. The GraphQL client and the Google login form both read this token. %>
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>
    <%= inertia_headers %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">

    <%#
      Ordering matters.

      vite_react_refresh_tag must come FIRST: it installs React Refresh's global hook,
      and any component module evaluated before that hook exists will not be
      hot-swappable (and React will warn about it). In production the helper renders
      nothing at all.

      Development: both helpers point at the Vite dev server (the `vite` container),
      which serves unbundled ES modules and opens an HMR websocket to the browser.
      Production: vite_javascript_tag reads public/vite/.vite/manifest.json and emits
      hashed, immutable asset URLs built at image build time. No Node runs in production.
    %>
    <%= vite_react_refresh_tag %>
    <%= vite_client_tag %>
    <%= vite_javascript_tag "application" %>
  </head>

  <body class="h-full bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 antialiased">
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
